attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a spine.** Columns 0 to 6, `proB` to `yafP`, are carried by 94 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 8% of calls {S1}. The model names 78 to 99.8% of them, fewest at column 6, `yafP`, 78% {S1}.

@variable **A fork follows at `yafO`**, column 7, carried by 66%, then variable column 8, `yafN`, 70% {S2.c7, S2.c8}. The spine returns at columns 15 to 20, `dpaA` to `yafV`, the stretch most in regions of plasticity, 22 to 46% {S7, P}. Through columns 22 to 51 a branch of 30 shell families runs in 15 to 17%, [[flagellar]] {S8.b22, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 92 against 89%, and hesitates less there, 0.48 against 0.55 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 22, a fork column, 2.19 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in variable columns.** Columns 68 to 79, `cdaR` to `fhuB`, are carried by 13 to 38%, all persistent {S8.c68-79}. The last column is `fhuB`, in 13% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 89% of genes**, 0.53 bits on average, perplexity 1.8 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.19 against 0.23 bits, and names fewer genes, 74% against 96% {C}.

